{"commit":"dca2baf","auditor":"blind-subagent LAP 5 (told nothing about laps 1-4)","recorded_by":"code-b, author, performed none of the five audits","at":"2026-09-21T00:40:00Z","found":15,"note":"LAP 5. Drew D5 and D6, both HIGH. D5: the commit message says the fix restores the author-cannot-audit check at the moment a claim is granted. IT DOES NOT -- claimJob compares the SESSION, which is still null on a failed lookup, and src/auditDispatch.mjs never reads author_source at all, so a transient git failure still made every seat eligible including the author's own. Third message of mine stated wider than its code on this one finding. What the fix DID buy is real and smaller: unavailable survives into the store so mergeQueue defers to a known author. D6: nothing asserted the call sites use the shared resolver -- reverting any of the three to a catch-to-null left the suite green, the precise regression the commit exists to prevent, recurring for the fourth consecutive lap. CONFIRMED TRUE: makeAuthorResolver itself is correct, all three call sites do use it, the four other auditJobsFor producers hand-roll nothing, and the sentinel cannot collide with a session id. D5 FIXED in 381bc6b, D6 in 381bc6b and 3eb87ca. Neither is audited."}
