{"commit":"7722f36","auditor":"blind-subagent LAP 4 (told nothing about laps 1-3)","recorded_by":"code-b, author, performed none of the four audits","at":"2026-09-20T23:30:00Z","found":16,"note":"LAP 4. Drew H3 and L15. The prologue claim 'Both are registered' was FALSE AT THIS COMMIT -- it touched neither list -- though 3ce08ab registered both immediately after, so it is not an open defect at HEAD; flagged because the range tip shipped a false assurance inside a control's own header. L15 (DERIVED): digest's claim to be insensitive to a missing trailing newline is false -- /\\n+$/ only matches when a newline is present, so a hook byte-identical to the template except for a missing final newline reports E_HOOK_INTEGRITY_TAMPERED. Rule 16: an alarm that fires on a clean hook is one people switch off. CONFIRMED TRUE: templates/hooks/post-commit cannot fail a commit -- every step is || exit 0 with a terminal exit 0. L15 REMAINS OPEN."}
{"commit":"553724b","auditor":"blind-subagent LAP 4 (told nothing about laps 1-3)","recorded_by":"code-b, author, performed none of the four audits","at":"2026-09-20T23:30:00Z","found":16,"note":"LAP 4. Drew H3 (HIGH): the hook attestation is STRUCTURALLY BLIND to core.hooksPath -- the exact threat its own prologue names. This commit replaced --git-path with --git-common-dir, which is unaffected by hooksPath, so the checker now validates <common>/hooks/post-commit UNCONDITIONALLY whether or not git would ever run it. The pre-commit fix would have honoured a real hooksPath had runGit not overridden it; this converted a recoverable bug into a permanent blind spot, and the result object carries NO caveat field, so a consumer reading ok:true concludes the hook surface is clean. The limitation IS written down -- in docs/STOP_GATE_HOOK_ATTESTATION.diff.md, outside this range, not in the script's prologue, output or return value. AND NOTHING CALLS THE SCRIPT: no npm script, no settings hook, no test, no module. Rule 17, 179 lines of detection with zero consumers. Only post-commit is checked; pre-commit, pre-push, commit-msg and prepare-commit-msg are not, and this repo's own hooks/pre-commit instructs readers to set core.hooksPath globally -- documenting the step that disarms the attestation. CONFIRMED TRUE: the diagnosis in this commit is correct, safeGit does pass core.hooksPath=/dev/null, and --git-common-dir is right in a linked worktree. H3 REMAINS OPEN."}
